A child joyfully riding atop a massive ceramic tiger statue in a whimsical Chinese garden setting, surrounded by fantastical mythological sculptures in vibrant primary colors, the scene rendered in Piet Mondrian's distinctive style with bold geometric blocks of red, yellow, and blue dividing the composition, the tiger fragmented into rectangular shapes while still maintaining its fierce form, black grid lines separating color fields, the 1930s theme park atmosphere translated into abstract planes and right angles, bright afternoon light creating sharp contrasts between the geometric sections.
